      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me check the working directory and existing compile script.Now I'll write the improved test with better understandability — clearer variable names, a descriptive test method name, and a comment explaining the intent.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`nulls0`, `nulls1`, `jsonSetter_Value0`) with descriptive names (`contentNullsHandling`, `setterValue`, `valueNullsHandling`) and renames the test method to `test_forContentNulls_doesNotAffectValueNulls`, making the intent immediately clear: `forContentNulls()` only sets content-null handling and leaves the value-nulls field at `DEFAULT`."
